\name{sc_run_subcluster}
\alias{sc_run_subcluster}
\title{Create an independently reviewed raw-count child from exact parent clusters}
\usage{
sc_run_subcluster(parent_project, child_project, clusters,
  parent_scope_hash, expected_parent_revision,
  strategy_proposal = NULL,
  choices = list(qc = "retain_selected", doublet = "keep",
    batch = "none", cycle = "none", reference = "none"),
  cycle_diagnostics = NULL, annotation_column = "sc_subtype",
  reviewer, reason, request_id, inherit_model = FALSE)
}
\arguments{
\item{parent_project}{Completed immutable parent project directory.}
\item{child_project}{New independent sibling project directory outside the parent, its outputs and symlinks. Its containing directory must exist.}
\item{clusters}{One or more exact literal cluster IDs from the parent scope inspector. Numeric child cluster labels are never used as parent cell identifiers.}
\item{parent_scope_hash, expected_parent_revision}{Exact whole-parent binding hash and revision from \code{sc_run_subcluster_scope}. Selection origin additionally freezes exact cell IDs and membership. Changed parents are refused.}
\item{strategy_proposal}{Complete typed \code{scagentkit.strategy.v1} plan, or NULL for a clearly labelled software starting plan. The default discloses resolution 0.4, seed 17, LogNormalize at 10000, at most 2000 expressed HVGs, at most 30 computed PCs bounded below the selected cell and requested HVG counts, at most 20 selected PCs and at most 30 UMAP neighbors. These are starting choices, not AI suggestions or biological optima. Supplied invalid settings are rejected rather than clipped or replaced.}
\item{choices}{Explicit named policies. QC defaults to \code{retain_selected}; this prohibits another cell filter. \code{review} permits a new supported typed filter in the one central child strategy review. Doublet supports \code{keep} only: source parent score metadata may be preserved but no refit or removal occurs. Batch defaults to \code{none}; \code{review} permits fresh explicit supported batch design review using the child's rebuilt PCA. Parent corrected embeddings are never inherited. Cycle defaults to \code{none}; \code{recompute} requires fresh child scoring settings and a new prefix before any reviewed regression. Reference defaults to \code{none}; \code{inherit} snapshots a saved parent reference with verified source hash and version and rederives candidates from current child markers.}
\item{cycle_diagnostics}{Explicit fresh scoring settings for \code{cycle = "recompute"}, including a declared gene set from \code{sc_cycle_gene_set} and a new column prefix. Existing parent scores retain their original reference provenance and do not authorize child regression.}
\item{annotation_column}{Fresh child annotation column. Parent old annotation columns are preserved as source metadata. The reserved fresh child cluster column is \code{sc_subcluster_clusters}.}
\item{reviewer, reason}{Nonempty analyst identity and selection rationale retained in creation history.}
\item{request_id}{Stable literal identifier of 1 through 128 letters, digits, periods, underscores or hyphens, beginning with a letter or digit. Reusing the same child path with the same request and settings is idempotent; mismatched requests are rejected.}
\item{inherit_model}{Explicit TRUE copies only the parent's safe immutable provider configuration, per-project budget and transfer policy at creation. No keys, callbacks or prior transfer approvals are inherited. Default FALSE remains manual with budget zero. Suggestions use \code{sc_run_suggest}; Continue remains local.}
}
\description{Freezes selected exact parent cell IDs and creates a fresh sparse raw-count Seurat input with source metadata aligned by cell ID. Child context inherits species and user facts. Parent normalization, scale data, reductions, graphs, active identities, cluster candidates and model history are not reused. The parent project and its files remain unchanged.}
\details{The child receives an independent project identity, parameters, deterministic seed, checksummed checkpoints and decision history. It uses the normal typed analysis pipeline and stops for one exact whole-strategy approval before cell filtering, normalization, PCA, neighbors or clustering. At least 21 selected cells and three expressed features are required for the supported fixed k=20 graph/PCA; there is no small-cohort or invalid-resolution fallback.

Creation holds parent and child locks continuously around an atomic initialization receipt and state publication. An orderly exception releases the owned locks, allowing the same literal request and payload to retry; a different request cannot reuse the path. A forcibly killed initializer may leave an abandoned lock. It is never automatically removed: verify its owner has stopped before explicit recovery. The existing \code{sc_run_unlock} requires a saved state and does not recover initialization before state publication. Every child Continue, resume and review checks its unchanged parent binding and original input scope. Local headless review is equivalent to the optional loopback workbench. By default the child is manual with budget zero and external transfer false. Explicit creation-time \code{inherit_model = TRUE} copies only safe provider metadata, the per-project budget and transfer policy; child accounting remains separate and no prior transfer approvals, callbacks or credentials are copied. The stage-only \code{sc_run_suggest} channel can preview and request suggestions under exact payload approval. Ordinary child Continue/resume remains provider-free; use \code{sc_run_suggest}, central scientific review and \code{sc_run_continue} for the equivalent headless path. Existing manual children cannot be reconfigured through the browser. Manual proposals and reviewed Unknown annotation remain supported.

Parent cycle/doublet score metadata may survive as verified source evidence when exact selected raw counts, feature IDs, cell IDs and score values match the saved parent artifact. They are not fresh child predictions. Fresh cycle recomputation is separately explicit and its applicability is checked inside the child strategy. Annotation reference inheritance requires a verified parent snapshot and declared version; no parent cluster-level evidence rows are transplanted.

Use \code{sc_run_subcluster_apply} after child annotation review to create a derived parent object with a fresh subtype column. Apply validates the exact approved retained child scope. Any explicit reviewed child QC exclusions are recorded separately from the frozen original selection; missing or unapproved cell IDs are refused. Existing parent objects and old annotation columns are preserved. See \code{docs/SUBCLUSTER_REVIEW.md} for scope, apply and undo boundaries.}
\value{Durable child status, pending whole-strategy proposal/hash, diagnostics and independent project identity. Creation does not approve its strategy or apply labels back to the parent.}
\seealso{\code{sc_run}, \code{sc_run_inspect}, \code{sc_run_approve}, \code{sc_run_continue}, \code{sc_run_subcluster_scope}, \code{sc_run_subcluster_apply}}
